  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 17.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">And sece man hundredes gemot be wíte, eallswa hit [riht] is to secenne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-a">And sece man hundredes gemot be wite, ealswa hit rih[t] is to seacan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et requiratur hundretum super witam, sicut iustum est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-b">Sece man his hundred. Séce man hundredes gemót be wíte, ealswa hit riht is to secanne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And sece man hundredes gemot be wite, eallswa hit is to secenne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">Everyone shall attend his hundred [court]. Everyone shall attend the hundred court, under pain of fine, whenever he is required by law to attend it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And everyone is to attend the hundred court whenever summoned or suffer a penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Besuche man sein Hundert. B) Und man besuche das Hundertschaftsgericht bei Strafe, so wie es richtig (fehlt G) ist zu besuchen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Let one attend one's hundred. B) And let the hundred-court be attended on pain of a fine, as it is right (lacking in G) to attend it.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="321"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 5</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5–5.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 17:1-18: III Eg 5-5:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘riht’ is supplied in G from the other MSS. B's heading is red. Liebermann compares III Eg 5.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">And . . . hundredes: Sece man his hundred B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hit is: hit riht is AB</note>
      </div>
    </body>
